1
00:00:05,410 --> 00:00:09,710
(Hwang In Youp)

2
00:00:09,810 --> 00:00:14,250
(Lee Hye Ri)

3
00:00:16,860 --> 00:00:21,460
(Baek Sung Chul, Lee Yul Eum)

4
00:00:35,010 --> 00:00:38,580
(Dream To You)

5
00:00:39,080 --> 00:00:40,080
(All people, events, and backgrounds are fictional.)

6
00:00:40,080 --> 00:00:41,080
(This drama includes footage created using AI.)

7
00:00:41,080 --> 00:00:42,080
(Children and animals were filmed under strict safety guidelines.)

8
00:00:43,980 --> 00:00:45,650
Do you think you're a flaw only in my life?

9
00:00:46,380 --> 00:00:47,390
Didn't you know?

10
00:00:47,590 --> 00:00:48,920
That you're the one who ruined her life?

11
00:00:49,920 --> 00:00:52,090
Woo Su Bin, you are my regret.

12
00:00:52,390 --> 00:00:53,460
You should go back to that day too,

13
00:00:54,430 --> 00:00:55,490
and see how I feel.

14
00:01:18,550 --> 00:01:19,550
What's wrong?

15
00:01:26,520 --> 00:01:27,530
This...

16
00:01:27,930 --> 00:01:28,930
Is this because of me?

17
00:01:30,960 --> 00:01:31,960
Tell me.

18
00:01:52,820 --> 00:01:54,650
Who said it was because of you?

19
00:01:59,660 --> 00:02:00,960
Did you ask me to come chasing after you?

20
00:02:01,730 --> 00:02:03,359
- Did you crash into me? - Joo Yi Jae.

21
00:02:03,360 --> 00:02:05,600
Be quiet. Your mother just fell asleep.

22
00:02:06,660 --> 00:02:07,670
Let's talk outside.

23
00:02:16,740 --> 00:02:18,610
(Episode 6)

24
00:02:22,250 --> 00:02:23,720
Were you never going to tell me?

25
00:02:24,550 --> 00:02:26,150
How could I? It was too humiliating.

26
00:02:27,090 --> 00:02:31,320
If you knew how much I liked you, you'd obviously get a huge ego.

27
00:02:31,720 --> 00:02:34,960
Gosh, I'd never want to see that. I can never tell you.

28
00:02:35,730 --> 00:02:36,730
The moment you saw me,

29
00:02:38,230 --> 00:02:40,370
you should've cursed me out or slapped me.

30
00:02:40,930 --> 00:02:41,930
Don't you remember?

31
00:02:42,570 --> 00:02:45,470
I did all of that. I cursed at you and slapped you.

32
00:02:46,370 --> 00:02:47,370
Joo Yi Jae.

33
00:02:48,440 --> 00:02:50,040
Don't talk about it like it's nothing.

34
00:02:51,780 --> 00:02:54,250
This might have just happened for you,

35
00:02:54,910 --> 00:02:56,610
but for me, it's been over ten years.

36
00:02:58,080 --> 00:03:00,590
I spent all that time blaming you.

37
00:03:01,090 --> 00:03:03,249
I guarantee if it weren't for my curse,

38
00:03:03,250 --> 00:03:04,990
you'd be even better off than you are now.

39
00:03:06,360 --> 00:03:07,790
How can you... Even in this situation...

40
00:03:08,260 --> 00:03:10,500
I lived with so much self-pity, and...

41
00:03:10,660 --> 00:03:12,500
it was only after meeting you again that I realised...

42
00:03:18,170 --> 00:03:20,440
I was actually blaming myself.

43
00:03:22,810 --> 00:03:24,180
That I couldn't forgive myself.

44
00:03:28,150 --> 00:03:29,150
I told you.

45
00:03:29,980 --> 00:03:30,980
My regret...

46
00:03:31,950 --> 00:03:33,720
- isn't you. It's me. - But still.

47
00:03:35,950 --> 00:03:36,960
What if I hadn't left?

48
00:03:37,120 --> 00:03:40,790
Then maybe it wouldn't have happened.

49
00:03:42,130 --> 00:03:43,190
But what are you going to do about it?

50
00:03:43,900 --> 00:03:46,200
What? Are you going to turn back time for me?

51
00:03:46,300 --> 00:03:48,370
Or are you going to erase my memories?

52
00:03:53,640 --> 00:03:54,640
I'm going to be sorry.

53
00:03:57,280 --> 00:03:59,739
I'll keep being sorry, regretful, and blaming myself.

54
00:03:59,740 --> 00:04:00,749
This is why I was afraid...

55
00:04:00,750 --> 00:04:01,950
Don't tell me I can't even do that.

56
00:04:05,320 --> 00:04:06,480
It's my burden to bear.

57
00:04:41,850 --> 00:04:43,890
It's not your fault, Su Bin.

58
00:04:47,060 --> 00:04:48,630
It's not your fault.

59
00:04:51,730 --> 00:04:53,260
It's okay.

60
00:05:20,760 --> 00:05:23,490
- You're up already? - You're up?

61
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:27,070
I'm an early riser. I always wake up at 5am.

62
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:31,170
You don't have to cook. Please rest, Mom.

63
00:05:32,670 --> 00:05:34,370
I want to do this for you.

64
00:05:35,640 --> 00:05:38,910
I'll leave it ready, so eat whenever you're hungry.

65
00:05:38,980 --> 00:05:41,280
- Where are you going? - I have to go home.

66
00:05:42,610 --> 00:05:45,380
Your father will be waking up soon.

67
00:05:46,850 --> 00:05:47,850
Mom.

68
00:05:49,850 --> 00:05:50,920
I brought your things.

69
00:05:51,990 --> 00:05:55,130
I brought a few outfits for now, so take a look...

70
00:05:55,360 --> 00:05:56,990
and let me know if you need anything else.

71
00:05:57,560 --> 00:05:58,700
Su Bin.

72
00:05:59,160 --> 00:06:02,670
Let's eat, Mom. It's been so long since I've had your cooking.

73
00:06:04,040 --> 00:06:05,100
Is this doenjang stew's smell?

74
00:06:10,910 --> 00:06:13,040
Okay, the one with the sun drawing on it...

75
00:06:13,110 --> 00:06:14,150
is for the morning.

76
00:06:14,910 --> 00:06:16,480
And after lunch...

77
00:06:18,950 --> 00:06:20,649
Since you'll take care of the flowerbed later,

78
00:06:20,650 --> 00:06:21,650
I'll draw a flower here.

79
00:06:22,590 --> 00:06:24,190
Gosh, you're a sharp one.

80
00:06:24,460 --> 00:06:26,460
If I'd known I was going to live this long,

81
00:06:26,560 --> 00:06:27,830
I would've learned how to read.

82
00:06:28,430 --> 00:06:29,690
It's not too late.

83
00:06:29,960 --> 00:06:31,600
I'll be dead soon anyway. What's the point?

84
00:06:32,060 --> 00:06:34,030
You used to say that back when I was a student.

85
00:06:35,930 --> 00:06:37,500
That's right. You're right. I did.

86
00:06:37,970 --> 00:06:40,200
The one with the crescent moon is for the evening.

87
00:06:40,270 --> 00:06:42,710
And for the one you take before bed...

88
00:06:42,770 --> 00:06:43,840
A smiley face.

89
00:06:44,580 --> 00:06:48,680
I love bedtime the most. So draw a big, happy smile.

90
00:06:49,210 --> 00:06:50,210
Okay.

91
00:06:50,211 --> 00:06:53,180
(Take Before Bed As Needed)

92
00:06:53,420 --> 00:06:55,050
I'm going to check on you when I get back from Seoul.

93
00:06:55,420 --> 00:06:58,390
- Make sure you take them. - All right, I will.

94
00:06:58,820 --> 00:06:59,860
If you collapse again,

95
00:07:00,160 --> 00:07:01,690
they said you could seriously injure your back.

96
00:07:02,230 --> 00:07:03,230
I know.

97
00:07:05,660 --> 00:07:06,660
Mom.

98
00:07:07,400 --> 00:07:08,970
You'll take good care of her, right?

99
00:07:10,570 --> 00:07:12,940
Of course. You can count on me.

100
00:07:13,810 --> 00:07:15,410
You just focus on your work.

101
00:07:16,140 --> 00:07:18,640
Goodness, with that delicate face of yours,

102
00:07:18,710 --> 00:07:21,050
who's taking care of whom? Forget it.

103
00:07:22,110 --> 00:07:24,080
My hands and feet are perfectly fine.

104
00:07:24,650 --> 00:07:26,480
You can work me as hard as you like.

105
00:07:35,460 --> 00:07:37,930
It's for the best. It was only a matter of time.

106
00:07:38,330 --> 00:07:40,700
- It's over. It's all over. - What's over?

107
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:42,000
What can he do?

108
00:07:42,370 --> 00:07:43,400
Is he going to run off to the States again?

109
00:07:43,900 --> 00:07:45,140
He convinced my daughter, who was doing just fine,

110
00:07:45,200 --> 00:07:46,200
to make a movie with him.

111
00:07:46,270 --> 00:07:47,670
He should see it through to the end.

112
00:07:48,310 --> 00:07:49,310
I mean...

113
00:07:50,070 --> 00:07:51,280
They have to make the movie together, sure.

114
00:07:51,980 --> 00:07:54,110
What I'm saying is that Su Bin's feelings...

115
00:07:54,180 --> 00:07:56,010
- are completely gone. - What feelings?

116
00:07:56,910 --> 00:07:57,920
Love.

117
00:07:58,480 --> 00:08:00,590
- Love. - Quit your nonsense and eat.

118
00:08:02,320 --> 00:08:03,320
Yi Jae.

119
00:08:03,920 --> 00:08:05,360
This is the irony of love.

120
00:08:06,360 --> 00:08:08,329
A woman will stay with a man who makes her cry,

121
00:08:08,330 --> 00:08:09,360
no matter what they tell her, right?

122
00:08:09,790 --> 00:08:13,360
But a man can't stay with a woman he makes cry.

123
00:08:14,600 --> 00:08:17,870
- Why? - Why? Because it's torture for him.

124
00:08:18,100 --> 00:08:21,170
His heart is breaking. But a real man, you know?

125
00:08:21,340 --> 00:08:22,940
He can't just sit there sobbing, can he?

126
00:08:23,640 --> 00:08:26,140
- That's what it means to be a man. - Yeong Jae.

127
00:08:26,510 --> 00:08:29,980
Joo Yeong Jae. Where did I go wrong raising you?

128
00:08:30,680 --> 00:08:31,720
It's all thanks to you, Mom.

129
00:08:32,320 --> 00:08:33,380
That wasn't a compliment.

130
00:08:39,090 --> 00:08:40,090
Hi.

131
00:08:42,490 --> 00:08:44,430
Do you still have the pins in your leg?

132
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:47,270
Hey. That's kind of a weird way to say good morning.

133
00:08:48,100 --> 00:08:51,400
I searched about it. It said you probably had a plate put in.

134
00:08:51,770 --> 00:08:54,010
I did. Just like the Iron Man.

135
00:08:55,040 --> 00:08:56,040
Why didn't you get it taken out?

136
00:08:56,540 --> 00:08:58,910
I couldn't get it removed. It's too close to a nerve,

137
00:08:58,980 --> 00:09:00,480
so they said it would be risky to operate.

138
00:09:00,910 --> 00:09:01,980
I see.

139
00:09:02,810 --> 00:09:05,350
Does it still bother you sometimes? When is it the worst?

140
00:09:06,350 --> 00:09:09,150
- Right now? - Now? Let me see.

141
00:09:09,890 --> 00:09:10,890
Where?

142
00:09:11,820 --> 00:09:13,020
Do you think you can figure out the problem just by looking at it?

143
00:09:13,960 --> 00:09:16,560
I need to know what's going on.

144
00:09:16,630 --> 00:09:18,860
It doesn't affect my daily life.

145
00:09:20,100 --> 00:09:21,430
So it never hurts or anything?

146
00:09:22,170 --> 00:09:24,800
Well, it throbs a little when it rains.

147
00:09:25,270 --> 00:09:27,140
It hurts a little if I walk or run a lot,

148
00:09:27,310 --> 00:09:28,310
especially at night.

149
00:09:29,270 --> 00:09:31,440
Does massaging it help? Are you taking any medication?

150
00:09:32,340 --> 00:09:34,910
Why are you writing that down? It's not bad enough for medication.

151
00:09:35,910 --> 00:09:38,520
On a scale from 0 to 10, how would you rate the pain?

152
00:09:38,880 --> 00:09:40,990
I don't know. It depends on my mood.

153
00:09:41,920 --> 00:09:43,350
Then I'd better keep you in a good mood.

154
00:09:45,060 --> 00:09:46,060
Just a second.

155
00:09:47,090 --> 00:09:48,090
What about back then?

156
00:09:49,360 --> 00:09:51,100
When you kissed me and ran away.

157
00:09:55,370 --> 00:09:58,170
Joo Yi Jae, are you crazy? Forget it. Stop following me.

158
00:09:58,240 --> 00:09:59,270
Joo Yi Jae, you'll get soaked.

159
00:10:01,770 --> 00:10:03,710
It was a sleepless night for many reasons.

160
00:10:05,640 --> 00:10:06,980
How? How much was it?

161
00:10:07,180 --> 00:10:08,180
On a scale of 0 to 10?

162
00:10:12,080 --> 00:10:13,080
- Just kidding. - Gosh.

163
00:10:13,720 --> 00:10:14,720
So...

164
00:10:15,090 --> 00:10:16,320
what can I do for you when it hurts?

165
00:10:16,450 --> 00:10:18,760
Nothing. I just endure it.

166
00:10:19,790 --> 00:10:20,860
I mean, how do you endure...

167
00:10:23,190 --> 00:10:24,200
See you later.

168
00:10:37,340 --> 00:10:38,340
Thanks.

169
00:11:00,970 --> 00:11:01,970
What are you doing?

170
00:11:02,470 --> 00:11:03,470
It's nothing.

171
00:11:06,200 --> 00:11:07,200
You've been uncomfortable, haven't you?

172
00:11:08,140 --> 00:11:09,470
- No... - Excuse me for a moment.

173
00:11:13,840 --> 00:11:14,880
- Gosh. -Why?

174
00:11:16,210 --> 00:11:19,720
- I'll do it. Don't worry. - Gosh, you...

175
00:11:24,190 --> 00:11:25,960
What? No.

176
00:11:28,490 --> 00:11:29,490
Mister.

177
00:11:30,290 --> 00:11:32,460
- What's all this? - Where should we install this?

178
00:11:32,530 --> 00:11:34,629
- What's... - Oh, you're here. Come on in.

179
00:11:34,630 --> 00:11:35,870
- Okay. - Joo Yi Jae, be careful.

180
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:38,200
- Hey, what is all this? - It's just something.

181
00:11:40,040 --> 00:11:41,040
Be careful.

182
00:11:46,340 --> 00:11:47,610
I was worried for nothing.

183
00:11:48,650 --> 00:11:50,880
Go on, try it out. I looked up all the reviews for this.

184
00:11:50,950 --> 00:11:52,020
This is supposed to be the best one.

185
00:11:53,480 --> 00:11:56,190
(Gyeongseong Love Song)

186
00:11:57,760 --> 00:12:01,460
I finally finished it.

187
00:12:01,660 --> 00:12:02,660
Great job.

188
00:12:03,330 --> 00:12:04,630
How did it feel to write again after so long?

189
00:12:04,730 --> 00:12:07,059
You know, writing is...

190
00:12:07,060 --> 00:12:08,070
like riding a bicycle.

191
00:12:08,570 --> 00:12:12,200
Once you get the hang of it, you never forget.

192
00:12:13,100 --> 00:12:14,110
Did I sound a little cocky just now?

193
00:12:15,040 --> 00:12:18,040
I guess you forgot everything about pulling your hair.

194
00:12:18,110 --> 00:12:19,110
No, I didn't.

195
00:12:19,180 --> 00:12:20,410
I also know this is just the beginning.

196
00:12:21,680 --> 00:12:25,150
Anyway, to celebrate finishing the first draft,

197
00:12:25,650 --> 00:12:26,650
how about a drink? Deal?

198
00:12:28,020 --> 00:12:29,020
Deal.

199
00:12:29,550 --> 00:12:31,460
(President Song of Taebaek)

200
00:12:31,690 --> 00:12:32,690
I'll get it out.

201
00:12:37,700 --> 00:12:39,860
- I didn't know you had this. - I brought them.

202
00:12:41,230 --> 00:12:43,670
It's like a trophy from my reporter days.

203
00:12:44,870 --> 00:12:47,469
- You've won a lot of awards. - As I feel happy now,

204
00:12:47,470 --> 00:12:48,510
you can pick what you want.

205
00:12:52,180 --> 00:12:53,810
(President Song of Taebaek)

206
00:12:54,080 --> 00:12:55,810
I want President Song of Taebaek.

207
00:12:56,180 --> 00:12:57,180
Okay.

208
00:12:58,780 --> 00:13:00,420
- Cheers. - Cheers.

209
00:13:04,090 --> 00:13:05,190
It's good, right?

210
00:13:05,590 --> 00:13:07,790
It's good, but it seems a little strong.

211
00:13:07,990 --> 00:13:10,230
I really never imagined you becoming a reporter.

212
00:13:10,490 --> 00:13:13,630
I didn't either. How many years was I a reporter?

213
00:13:14,470 --> 00:13:17,540
I climbed a tree one day. A really old tree.

214
00:13:17,600 --> 00:13:19,940
They said I couldn't have it, so I tried to steal it.

215
00:13:22,140 --> 00:13:24,240
What's your best scene?

216
00:13:24,580 --> 00:13:27,710
That arrogance of yours showing that this will probably do well too?

217
00:13:27,780 --> 00:13:31,650
That just because I've gotten famous, or something...

218
00:13:31,720 --> 00:13:33,020
That will never happen.

219
00:13:33,080 --> 00:13:35,190
That's just because you're so cocky.

220
00:14:11,460 --> 00:14:15,730
(Gyeongseong Love Song)

221
00:14:15,790 --> 00:14:18,260
(Written and Directed by Woo Su Bin and Joo Yi Jae)

222
00:14:21,270 --> 00:14:23,100
Gosh.

223
00:14:24,300 --> 00:14:27,370
Director, this place looks completely different from before.

224
00:14:27,540 --> 00:14:29,110
The studio is so nice.

225
00:14:29,740 --> 00:14:31,040
For a housewarming gift for a place like this,

226
00:14:31,110 --> 00:14:32,110
is toilet paper okay?

227
00:14:32,680 --> 00:14:35,750
- Of course. - Billionaires use toilet paper.

228
00:14:36,950 --> 00:14:39,220
Thank you. But where's the DP?

229
00:14:42,050 --> 00:14:43,550
Hey, Director Woo.

230
00:14:45,060 --> 00:14:47,660
(Director of Photography)

231
00:14:47,890 --> 00:14:48,930
Director.

232
00:14:49,630 --> 00:14:51,630
- It's been a while. - You've been well?

233
00:14:51,730 --> 00:14:53,100
Do you still like gummies?

234
00:14:53,160 --> 00:14:55,870
- My hands shake without these. - Oh my.

235
00:14:55,930 --> 00:14:58,400
Thanks to the script you sent, the trip here wasn't boring.

236
00:14:58,700 --> 00:15:00,240
I'm sorry. Are you still jet-lagged?

237
00:15:00,300 --> 00:15:02,240
Well, I just came thinking of it as a vacation.

238
00:15:02,940 --> 00:15:04,380
But on my way here, I realised...

239
00:15:04,440 --> 00:15:06,440
I've been here before, about 20 years ago.

240
00:15:06,510 --> 00:15:08,550
You shot Silent Waves here, don't you remember?

241
00:15:09,350 --> 00:15:12,620
(Lighting Director)

242
00:15:12,680 --> 00:15:13,750
You scared me.

243
00:15:14,250 --> 00:15:15,320
Oh, you must be the lighting director.

244
00:15:15,390 --> 00:15:17,390
Yes, that's right. I'm Kim Gwang Il, in charge of lighting.

245
00:15:17,450 --> 00:15:18,860
It's Gwang for "light" and Il for "one."

246
00:15:19,290 --> 00:15:23,330
Oh my, hello. I'm Shin Seok Gi, in charge of sound.

247
00:15:23,630 --> 00:15:27,360
(Sound Recordist)

248
00:15:32,940 --> 00:15:37,540
(Art Director)

249
00:15:37,740 --> 00:15:41,180
- I'm Namgung Se Ra, Art Director. - Hello.

250
00:15:42,280 --> 00:15:45,420
Thank you all so much for coming all this way. Really.

251
00:15:45,480 --> 00:15:47,420
But where is Joo Yi Jae?

252
00:15:47,790 --> 00:15:49,220
Oh, Director Joo Yi Jae is...

253
00:15:50,950 --> 00:15:52,590
A staff meeting, all of a sudden?

254
00:15:53,360 --> 00:15:55,130
I'm not mentally prepared for this yet.

255
00:15:57,660 --> 00:16:00,200
Why is my GPS not functioning?

256
00:16:01,730 --> 00:16:03,030
Excuse me.

257
00:16:05,900 --> 00:16:08,210
Excuse me. Excuse me.

258
00:16:08,940 --> 00:16:09,940
What do you want?

259
00:16:10,210 --> 00:16:11,980
I was just going to ask for directions.

260
00:16:12,040 --> 00:16:14,750
- Who asks directions these days? - Seriously.

261
00:16:15,980 --> 00:16:17,410
Director Joo Yi Jae.

262
00:16:19,050 --> 00:16:20,050
Who are you?

263
00:16:20,880 --> 00:16:24,520
(Assistant Director)

264
00:16:24,590 --> 00:16:27,420
I'm Ryu Sang Mok, the Assistant Director.

265
00:16:28,830 --> 00:16:31,100
- I'm sorry. I'm so sorry. - That hurts...

266
00:16:31,160 --> 00:16:33,260
- Are you okay? - That hurts. Really.

267
00:16:34,730 --> 00:16:36,300
You grabbed me so suddenly, so I...

268
00:16:36,730 --> 00:16:38,800
- You suddenly twisted it... - Oh, I'm so sorry.

269
00:16:40,500 --> 00:16:42,240
- Please, this way. - That's right.

270
00:16:42,510 --> 00:16:45,240
- Yes, hello everyone. - Welcome, AD.

271
00:16:45,640 --> 00:16:46,710
The public parking lot is quite far, right?

272
00:16:47,010 --> 00:16:48,810
Yes, I got completely lost.

273
00:16:49,380 --> 00:16:51,520
I ran into Director Joo just outside.

274
00:16:54,890 --> 00:16:55,890
Director Joo?

275
00:16:56,390 --> 00:16:58,720
Hello. It's nice to meet you all.

276
00:16:58,790 --> 00:17:02,960
- My name is Joo Yi Jae. - Well, at least I get to see you.

277
00:17:03,490 --> 00:17:04,500
Good to see you.

278
00:17:04,730 --> 00:17:06,100
Well, how about we save the introductions...

279
00:17:06,260 --> 00:17:08,870
for after the location hunting?

280
00:17:09,330 --> 00:17:10,700
- We have to go. - Location scouting. Now?

281
00:17:10,770 --> 00:17:14,200
- Hurry up. We're busy. Let's go. - Let's go. Let's get going.

282
00:17:14,270 --> 00:17:15,870
See you later, Director Joo.

283
00:17:16,310 --> 00:17:18,140
Location scouting, right now?

284
00:17:20,810 --> 00:17:22,450
Excuse me, just a moment.

285
00:17:24,420 --> 00:17:25,450
Give me a second.

286
00:17:27,720 --> 00:17:28,720
Just a moment, please.

287
00:17:35,190 --> 00:17:36,190
Why?

288
00:17:36,760 --> 00:17:38,500
Weren't we supposed to have a script meeting today?

289
00:17:39,030 --> 00:17:41,300
Yes, we are. While I'm out scouting,

290
00:17:41,370 --> 00:17:42,930
you can have the meeting with the producers.

291
00:17:43,230 --> 00:17:44,330
Why am I not going?

292
00:17:45,570 --> 00:17:46,570
Well, there are two directors.

293
00:17:46,640 --> 00:17:47,870
It's better if we divide and conquer.

294
00:17:47,940 --> 00:17:49,310
You said we'd do everything together.

295
00:17:49,940 --> 00:17:51,180
If we're scouting the locations,

296
00:17:51,280 --> 00:17:52,580
that means we'll definitely be hiking.

297
00:17:52,910 --> 00:17:54,849
Don't tell me you're leaving me behind...

298
00:17:54,850 --> 00:17:56,410
because you're worried my legs will hurt.

299
00:17:56,580 --> 00:17:57,610
That's not it.

300
00:17:58,280 --> 00:18:00,580
- I'll check out the sets too. - That's not what I meant.

301
00:18:00,650 --> 00:18:01,650
Yi Jae,

302
00:18:02,620 --> 00:18:04,050
I think this is for the best.

303
00:18:06,720 --> 00:18:08,890
Let's just do it this way. Let's not talk about it anymore.

304
00:18:11,560 --> 00:18:12,560
I'm going.

305
00:18:19,470 --> 00:18:23,270
- Up ahead... - How many steps will we clock?

306
00:18:23,370 --> 00:18:27,079
- Obvi. We'll easily pass 30,000. - What's "obvi?"

307
00:18:27,080 --> 00:18:28,580
What?

308
00:18:28,780 --> 00:18:30,780
- It means "obviously." - Jeez.

309
00:18:31,380 --> 00:18:32,380
Gosh, my knees are killing me.

310
00:18:32,450 --> 00:18:33,780
The people who aren't going are so lucky.

311
00:18:33,850 --> 00:18:34,990
Right, Sang Mok?

312
00:18:35,150 --> 00:18:37,390
Come on, but this location scouting...

313
00:18:37,490 --> 00:18:39,860
is the highlight of pre-production, isn't it?

314
00:18:39,920 --> 00:18:42,560
I'm honoured to be a part of it, Lighting Director.

315
00:18:42,630 --> 00:18:47,200
- If hurt, don't be a burden. - That's a "burd."

316
00:18:47,660 --> 00:18:49,669
Hey, why would you say something so hurtful, DP?

317
00:18:49,670 --> 00:18:51,070
I feel sad to hear that.

318
00:18:51,400 --> 00:18:52,400
Gwang Il's feelings are hurt.

319
00:18:53,140 --> 00:18:54,970
Be safe.

320
00:18:56,210 --> 00:18:58,280
Have a good meeting. And just in case...

321
00:19:00,380 --> 00:19:01,880
Call me if anything comes up.

322
00:19:03,010 --> 00:19:04,820
- Okay. - Don't worry.

323
00:19:05,950 --> 00:19:07,720
- Have a safe trip. - Be safe.

324
00:19:17,760 --> 00:19:21,169
Okay, the scene list is finalised. Next...

325
00:19:21,170 --> 00:19:22,300
- Here. - Okay.

326
00:19:33,710 --> 00:19:36,980
Okay, next I'll share the directing team's feedback.

327
00:19:59,500 --> 00:20:00,540
Are you okay?

328
00:20:05,940 --> 00:20:07,380
Shouldn't you go to the hospital?

329
00:20:08,850 --> 00:20:10,010
Oh, I'm fine.

330
00:20:30,170 --> 00:20:31,769
I thought you died on the way.

331
00:20:31,770 --> 00:20:33,740
I ordered ages ago, and it still says you're on your way.

332
00:20:35,040 --> 00:20:36,440
Yes, the accident has been reported.

333
00:20:36,840 --> 00:20:38,440
Since this will be processed as a customer refund,

334
00:20:38,510 --> 00:20:40,010
the delivery fee will not be paid.

335
00:20:42,250 --> 00:20:43,950
Are you okay? You're not badly hurt?

336
00:20:44,850 --> 00:20:45,850
What about the repair costs?

337
00:20:46,620 --> 00:20:47,990
If you don't have the money, I can lend you some.

338
00:21:34,430 --> 00:21:37,200
(Grandma's Grilled Fish)

339
00:21:41,410 --> 00:21:42,410
Gosh, it's salty.

340
00:21:47,480 --> 00:21:49,380
Ma'am, this is what you mentioned last time.

341
00:21:54,180 --> 00:21:56,990
So, the guy Ha Na was looking for...

342
00:21:58,420 --> 00:21:59,760
and the guy from the shin-kicking incident...

343
00:22:01,360 --> 00:22:03,760
- They are all the same guy? - Yes.

344
00:22:05,200 --> 00:22:07,160
(Sim Yu Geon)

345
00:22:10,870 --> 00:22:11,870
Interesting.

346
00:22:14,440 --> 00:22:17,140
Should I get the grilled fish?

347
00:22:18,310 --> 00:22:19,910
Ma'am, the soup was way too salty today.

348
00:22:21,480 --> 00:22:22,610
Come on, ma'am.

349
00:22:25,620 --> 00:22:27,520
You ate it all, so why the attitude now?

350
00:22:41,930 --> 00:22:42,930
Hey.

351
00:22:42,931 --> 00:22:43,969
(Nerve-racking Woman, Trembling Man)

352
00:22:43,970 --> 00:22:44,970
You're really doing this?

353
00:22:45,240 --> 00:22:48,340
I heard CEO Ahn is doting on Director Kim these days...

354
00:22:48,410 --> 00:22:50,640
to cast you in that "nerve-racking woman" role.

355
00:22:51,680 --> 00:22:53,910
Your mama's working so hard.

356
00:22:54,610 --> 00:22:56,050
What's next? Is she going to bribe everyone with burgers?

357
00:22:56,410 --> 00:22:58,420
This is so immature. It's making my ears bleed.

358
00:23:00,380 --> 00:23:01,750
What does that have to do with you?

359
00:23:01,820 --> 00:23:03,349
Of course it does have something to do with me.

360
00:23:03,350 --> 00:23:04,760
I got dropped from this project because of you.

361
00:23:04,820 --> 00:23:06,920
I was supposed to be the "trembling man."

362
00:23:07,190 --> 00:23:09,030
But after the rumours about our fight got out,

363
00:23:09,830 --> 00:23:12,300
- I became Oh Ha Na's ashtray. - But I don't smoke.

364
00:23:14,970 --> 00:23:17,070
I was first in line, you know?

365
00:23:17,370 --> 00:23:19,269
I had my meeting with the director ages ago.

366
00:23:19,270 --> 00:23:20,400
We were all done with it.

367
00:23:20,470 --> 00:23:23,140
If you got cut because of me, someone who hasn't read the script,

368
00:23:23,470 --> 00:23:24,509
doesn't that say more about you?

369
00:23:24,510 --> 00:23:26,839
What are you talking about? I heard you begged the director,

370
00:23:26,840 --> 00:23:28,980
- and sent a handwritten letter. - What a joke.

371
00:23:31,050 --> 00:23:33,250
See? This is all part of CEO Ahn's plan.

372
00:23:33,380 --> 00:23:35,920
This is why you're just living in your own little paradise...

373
00:23:35,990 --> 00:23:37,619
while there's a war zone out here.

374
00:23:37,620 --> 00:23:39,820
Must be nice, right? Really nice.

375
00:23:39,890 --> 00:23:42,130
The world must look so beautiful to you.

376
00:23:42,190 --> 00:23:43,930
If you're that jealous, you can have it. I'm serious.

377
00:23:43,990 --> 00:23:45,560
Have what? CEO Ahn?

378
00:23:51,230 --> 00:23:53,540
- "Trembling man." It's yours. - What?

379
00:23:53,700 --> 00:23:55,410
I'm not planning on staying here much longer.

380
00:23:57,510 --> 00:23:58,510
I'm escaping.

381
00:23:59,110 --> 00:24:00,840
What do you mean? Escaping?

382
00:24:01,780 --> 00:24:03,810
Is skipping the wrap party your idea of an escape?

383
00:24:05,320 --> 00:24:08,020
- Are you a fool? Get out. - Am I?

384
00:24:08,390 --> 00:24:10,220
I'm taking this, okay? I'm really doing it.

385
00:24:11,090 --> 00:24:12,390
You said you didn't want it, right? I'm taking it.

386
00:24:13,020 --> 00:24:14,090
Don't you go back on your word.

387
00:24:14,360 --> 00:24:15,360
I'm really doing it, okay?

388
00:24:22,400 --> 00:24:24,700
Time for a group photo. Everyone, please gather around.

389
00:24:24,870 --> 00:24:27,200
- Hurry up, come on. - Okay, let's get in position.

390
00:24:27,640 --> 00:24:28,640
Let's take it quickly.

391
00:24:28,970 --> 00:24:29,970
Gosh.

392
00:24:31,880 --> 00:24:33,380
- Who are you looking for? - People in front, please sit down.

393
00:24:34,310 --> 00:24:36,350
- Where is Yu Geon? - Here...

394
00:24:36,580 --> 00:24:38,249
- Who's Yu Geon? - Please stand there...

395
00:24:38,250 --> 00:24:40,879
- Please sit down quickly. - Gang Member three.

396
00:24:40,880 --> 00:24:44,350
- Gang Member three? He died. - People in the back...

397
00:24:44,490 --> 00:24:46,419
- Please come here. It'd be better. - When?

398
00:24:46,420 --> 00:24:48,490
- On your day off. - Please...

399
00:24:51,060 --> 00:24:52,100
So he's dead.

400
00:25:04,570 --> 00:25:07,110
(The food of Simsim Seafood can be served through takeout or delivery.)

401
00:25:08,210 --> 00:25:10,550
It's time you quit and come back home.

402
00:25:11,650 --> 00:25:14,620
You've been at it long enough. Come home...

403
00:25:15,250 --> 00:25:16,390
and learn the family business.

404
00:25:17,090 --> 00:25:18,620
We haven't seen each other in two years.

405
00:25:21,020 --> 00:25:23,630
Couldn't you at least ask how I've been or if I've eaten?

406
00:25:23,830 --> 00:25:27,200
Am I asking you to take care of me when I'm sick?

407
00:25:27,700 --> 00:25:29,000
Am I asking you for money?

408
00:25:29,730 --> 00:25:31,299
I'm telling you to take this business.

409
00:25:31,300 --> 00:25:33,500
I'm telling you, I don't want to.

410
00:25:33,570 --> 00:25:35,070
And you think you enjoy being a delivery driver?

411
00:25:35,770 --> 00:25:38,480
Whenever I see a motorcycle accident on the news,

412
00:25:38,540 --> 00:25:39,740
my heart sinks.

413
00:25:41,540 --> 00:25:43,580
Yu Geon, holding out like this...

414
00:25:44,250 --> 00:25:46,220
isn't persistence. It's just stubbornness.

415
00:25:47,280 --> 00:25:48,290
No.

416
00:25:49,850 --> 00:25:50,890
I can do it.

417
00:25:52,390 --> 00:25:55,160
I don't want to be left with a regret like your guitar, Dad.

418
00:25:57,990 --> 00:25:59,000
Why did you come here?

419
00:26:00,800 --> 00:26:02,070
Did you just come to upset me?

420
00:26:04,800 --> 00:26:05,870
I just...

421
00:26:09,070 --> 00:26:10,670
I came because I missed you, Dad.

422
00:26:21,620 --> 00:26:23,150
But there's something I have to say before I go.

423
00:26:25,390 --> 00:26:26,390
I...

424
00:26:28,560 --> 00:26:31,090
I'm never going to quit. No, I can't quit.

425
00:26:33,860 --> 00:26:34,930
I'm sorry, Dad.

426
00:26:40,470 --> 00:26:41,500
That little punk.

427
00:26:49,180 --> 00:26:50,410
(Open, Takeout Available)

428
00:26:50,510 --> 00:26:51,850
You have one month.

429
00:26:53,020 --> 00:26:54,220
If you don't come back,

430
00:26:54,350 --> 00:26:55,950
I'll go to Seoul and drag you home myself.

431
00:26:56,020 --> 00:26:57,050
You hear me?

432
00:26:58,920 --> 00:27:01,890
(Open, Takeout Available)

433
00:27:47,400 --> 00:27:48,809
You know your dad's just worried about you,

434
00:27:48,810 --> 00:27:49,870
right?

435
00:27:52,480 --> 00:27:53,980
He might not show it,

436
00:27:54,080 --> 00:27:55,610
but he watches every single thing you're in.

437
00:27:56,480 --> 00:27:58,419
I don't even know what you're in.

438
00:27:58,420 --> 00:28:02,720
But he knows all the terms...

439
00:28:02,790 --> 00:28:04,620
from close-ups to bust shots.

440
00:28:04,690 --> 00:28:05,820
What good does that do?

441
00:28:06,790 --> 00:28:08,020
All he ever does is tell me to come home.

442
00:28:09,530 --> 00:28:12,300
Hey. Come on, you're Sim Yu Geon, Kaneshiro Takeshi of Saero High.

443
00:28:12,500 --> 00:28:15,130
You're the face of our town. Why are you so discouraged?

444
00:28:15,930 --> 00:28:17,430
Kaneshiro Takeshi? That's nonsense.

445
00:28:18,840 --> 00:28:19,900
When I went to Seoul,

446
00:28:21,000 --> 00:28:22,910
I saw guys better-looking than me are a dime a dozen.

447
00:28:22,970 --> 00:28:26,510
Don't lie. Are you just teasing me because I've never been to Seoul?

448
00:28:27,340 --> 00:28:28,610
Hey, I can speak in a Seoul accent too, you know.

449
00:28:31,450 --> 00:28:32,480
Have you eaten?

450
00:28:33,550 --> 00:28:34,550
Alright.

451
00:28:35,050 --> 00:28:37,150
- Just focus on driving. - Have you eaten?

452
00:28:39,460 --> 00:28:41,560
(Bunam Intercity Bus Terminal)

453
00:28:41,760 --> 00:28:42,860
We're here. Get out.

454
00:28:44,360 --> 00:28:45,360
Thanks.

455
00:28:48,000 --> 00:28:49,000
Oh, right.

456
00:28:49,600 --> 00:28:50,600
Hey, take this.

457
00:28:52,570 --> 00:28:54,070
- What is it? - Your dad told me to give you this.

458
00:28:57,240 --> 00:28:58,270
Hey, I'm taking off.

459
00:28:58,540 --> 00:28:59,979
Hey, hey, Joo Yeong Jae.

460
00:28:59,980 --> 00:29:03,750
(Bunam Intercity Bus Terminal)

461
00:29:11,590 --> 00:29:15,430
(Bunam Intercity Bus Terminal)

462
00:29:20,800 --> 00:29:22,530
- Hello? - Hello?

463
00:29:23,230 --> 00:29:24,830
Is this Sim Yu Geon?

464
00:29:25,740 --> 00:29:26,900
Yes, speaking.

465
00:29:27,670 --> 00:29:28,670
Who's this?

466
00:29:29,340 --> 00:29:30,610
It's me, Director Kang.

467
00:29:42,190 --> 00:29:44,750
Gosh, this location manager is the worst.

468
00:29:45,120 --> 00:29:47,720
I told him not to show the director this place,

469
00:29:48,020 --> 00:29:49,730
and I was clear that we'd need at least ten PA.

470
00:29:50,430 --> 00:29:52,659
Do you know how much money that'll cost?

471
00:29:52,660 --> 00:29:56,270
Exactly. I'm sure they left it on the list on purpose.

472
00:29:56,570 --> 00:29:58,400
Because they knew he'd approve it the moment he visits there.

473
00:29:59,070 --> 00:30:00,900
They just didn't want to bother scouting other locations.

474
00:30:01,070 --> 00:30:02,910
Those devious schemers.

475
00:30:04,010 --> 00:30:05,040
Director Joo.

476
00:30:05,640 --> 00:30:07,610
Could you please talk to him?

477
00:30:08,040 --> 00:30:10,310
Pardon? Well, I...

478
00:30:11,050 --> 00:30:14,450
- I'm not familiar with this. - What?

479
00:30:16,450 --> 00:30:18,290
These location photos we're looking at...

480
00:30:20,690 --> 00:30:23,390
(Gyeongseong Love Song Location Team)

481
00:30:26,230 --> 00:30:28,230
Producer, she's not here.

482
00:30:29,070 --> 00:30:30,100
I said she's not here.

483
00:30:32,940 --> 00:30:33,940
What?

484
00:30:34,900 --> 00:30:36,870
Are you not in this chat room?

485
00:30:37,470 --> 00:30:38,780
No, I'm not.

486
00:30:40,140 --> 00:30:41,140
I'm sorry.

487
00:30:41,740 --> 00:30:43,910
- AD Sang Mok made this chat, right? - Yes.

488
00:30:44,480 --> 00:30:46,749
I'll invite you right now. Gosh.

489
00:30:46,750 --> 00:30:49,119
No, that's okay, Producer. It's just...

490
00:30:49,120 --> 00:30:50,750
Director Woo might have done it...

491
00:30:50,820 --> 00:30:52,490
because he didn't want to disturb my writing.

492
00:30:52,790 --> 00:30:54,360
I'll get what I need from him directly.

493
00:30:54,560 --> 00:30:56,030
That could be why.

494
00:30:57,660 --> 00:30:58,900
I was spooked.

495
00:31:00,430 --> 00:31:01,800
Seriously.

496
00:31:03,070 --> 00:31:04,500
Why did he have to go there?

497
00:31:07,170 --> 00:31:09,810
Director, we're heading out for the day.

498
00:31:10,140 --> 00:31:13,640
Isn't the commute a hassle? If you don't mind,

499
00:31:13,710 --> 00:31:16,109
- you're welcome to sleep here. - Oh, no, it's fine.

500
00:31:16,110 --> 00:31:17,880
You should have a rest with no stress.

501
00:31:18,180 --> 00:31:22,420
- Our place is really close by. - I live close by too, so...

502
00:31:23,390 --> 00:31:25,790
- We'll get going then. - We'll get going.

503
00:31:25,860 --> 00:31:28,929
- Oh, okay. - See you tomorrow.

504
00:31:28,930 --> 00:31:31,030
- Good work today. - Good work.

505
00:31:41,700 --> 00:31:43,239
- What's this? - Seriously?

506
00:31:43,240 --> 00:31:44,639
- That's not funny at all. - Please stop...

507
00:31:44,640 --> 00:31:46,240
with those kinds of jokes.

508
00:31:51,650 --> 00:31:55,720
Director. We were going to our place, and we just stopped by...

509
00:31:55,790 --> 00:31:57,120
Oh, yes.

510
00:31:57,920 --> 00:32:00,960
- Could you have a seat? - Just a moment.

511
00:32:03,560 --> 00:32:05,089
- Hello? - Yi Jae.

512
00:32:05,090 --> 00:32:06,900
We're getting chicken. You in?

513
00:32:06,960 --> 00:32:09,029
- I'm on my way now. - Where are you going? What?

514
00:32:09,030 --> 00:32:11,269
- I have plans as well. - Oh, okay.

515
00:32:11,270 --> 00:32:14,540
- What? You mean you'll join? - Just order it first.

516
00:32:14,600 --> 00:32:17,270
You're supposed to order. Please order original fried chicken.

517
00:32:21,440 --> 00:32:22,610
Did you order the chicken?

518
00:32:23,050 --> 00:32:24,610
Chicken? Don't be ridiculous.

519
00:32:25,080 --> 00:32:26,350
So you didn't order?

520
00:32:29,120 --> 00:32:31,890
Seriously, why is she being like this again?

521
00:32:42,730 --> 00:32:44,800
My legs...

522
00:32:48,240 --> 00:32:49,240
Gosh.

523
00:32:49,241 --> 00:32:50,540
- Hey, Gwang Il. - Yes?

524
00:32:53,180 --> 00:32:57,950
Well, everyone. I know you're tired, but let's have a quick meeting.

525
00:32:58,250 --> 00:32:59,620
Things can't go on like this.

526
00:33:07,820 --> 00:33:08,829
Let's go.

527
00:33:08,830 --> 00:33:09,860
(Munak Mountain)

528
00:33:10,430 --> 00:33:12,560
These locations we've scouted over the past few days...

529
00:33:12,630 --> 00:33:14,060
Are they really the best we can do?

530
00:33:14,300 --> 00:33:17,000
I know it's not easy to shoot a period piece on this budget.

531
00:33:17,130 --> 00:33:18,739
But I don't want to just shoot at some mediocre location and...

532
00:33:18,740 --> 00:33:22,210
- try to fix it in post-production. - That's right.

533
00:33:22,610 --> 00:33:23,610
Right.

534
00:33:24,170 --> 00:33:27,410
- We have our pride to think about. - We have to do better.

535
00:33:28,110 --> 00:33:29,210
We need to do more legwork.

536
00:33:29,680 --> 00:33:32,380
Assistant Director, search the area around the set again.

537
00:33:32,780 --> 00:33:36,020
No residents, no tourists, no power lines...

538
00:33:41,590 --> 00:33:42,759
No power lines, no buildings in the shot,

539
00:33:42,760 --> 00:33:45,500
and somewhere with good lighting. You know what I mean, right?

540
00:33:45,560 --> 00:33:47,899
I get what you're saying, but you also said...

541
00:33:47,900 --> 00:33:49,770
we can't use locations that are too recognizable.

542
00:33:50,630 --> 00:33:52,029
If that's the case, a place like that doesn't exist.

543
00:33:52,030 --> 00:33:54,299
No. Either it exists, or we haven't found it yet.

544
00:33:54,300 --> 00:33:55,370
It's 1 of 2 things.

545
00:33:55,440 --> 00:33:56,440
It's not that it doesn't exist.

546
00:33:56,710 --> 00:33:59,240
- Let me see. - Director.

547
00:34:00,340 --> 00:34:02,179
- You're here. - Please let me see...

548
00:34:02,180 --> 00:34:05,010
I thought they were coming tomorrow.

549
00:34:05,210 --> 00:34:07,820
The landowner suddenly didn't allow them to use the land.

550
00:34:07,980 --> 00:34:09,619
So they wrapped things up and came.

551
00:34:09,620 --> 00:34:12,920
- I see. - Okay.

552
00:34:13,690 --> 00:34:16,290
It's too cramped, so it would be hard to film there.

553
00:34:30,740 --> 00:34:31,840
Where did everyone go?

554
00:34:32,940 --> 00:34:34,880
Back to their places. I sent them all away.

555
00:34:35,480 --> 00:34:38,050
Why? Do you want to be alone?

556
00:34:38,880 --> 00:34:41,080
- Should I go too? - Of course not.

557
00:34:41,220 --> 00:34:42,450
I sent them because I want to be only with you.

558
00:34:42,920 --> 00:34:44,150
How was the meeting?

559
00:34:44,650 --> 00:34:46,090
Not bad.

560
00:34:47,320 --> 00:34:48,789
Have a seat. You haven't seen the photos,

561
00:34:48,790 --> 00:34:49,830
have you?

562
00:34:57,130 --> 00:34:58,130
This place is perfect,

563
00:34:58,200 --> 00:35:00,000
but we can't get cars in, so we dropped it.

564
00:35:00,970 --> 00:35:02,209
And for this one, when we got there,

565
00:35:02,210 --> 00:35:03,310
there wasn't enough space to work with.

566
00:35:04,240 --> 00:35:05,370
So this one is the best option we have.

567
00:35:05,980 --> 00:35:06,980
What do you think?

568
00:35:13,920 --> 00:35:15,420
Are you really curious about my opinion?

569
00:35:17,690 --> 00:35:19,619
- What? - Nod if you like it,

570
00:35:19,620 --> 00:35:20,620
shake your head if you don't.

571
00:35:21,360 --> 00:35:22,390
What should I do?

572
00:35:23,390 --> 00:35:25,630
- I'll do whatever you say. - Why are you being like this?

573
00:35:26,100 --> 00:35:27,860
Even the person who saw it in person can't make a decision.

574
00:35:27,960 --> 00:35:30,830
Who am I to say if it's good or not?

575
00:35:32,740 --> 00:35:33,969
I'm too ashamed to even face the crew...

576
00:35:33,970 --> 00:35:35,240
who went through all that trouble.

577
00:35:37,310 --> 00:35:39,239
I already spoke to them and arranged it...

578
00:35:39,240 --> 00:35:40,440
What did you say to them?

579
00:35:40,940 --> 00:35:42,580
That Joo Yi Jae is my first love,

580
00:35:42,880 --> 00:35:46,220
that we have a special relationship, so I want to be considerate? Or...

581
00:35:46,920 --> 00:35:49,890
That I wanted to exclude her from difficult tasks...

582
00:35:50,790 --> 00:35:53,260
since her leg is bad now because of me

583
00:35:53,720 --> 00:35:56,089
Why? Did someone say something to you?

584
00:35:56,090 --> 00:35:59,830
No, no one has said anything. Don't you find that strange?

585
00:36:00,560 --> 00:36:04,030
No one asks who I am, and how or why I'm here as a director.

586
00:36:08,540 --> 00:36:09,540
Why do you think that is?

587
00:36:16,510 --> 00:36:17,510
Yi Jae.

588
00:36:18,250 --> 00:36:19,280
Joo Yi Jae.

589
00:36:31,890 --> 00:36:34,630
What's wrong with me? Gosh.

590
00:36:34,900 --> 00:36:36,630
I didn't even cry when I won the grand prize.

591
00:36:40,440 --> 00:36:42,000
But why is this so sad?

592
00:36:48,910 --> 00:36:51,210
But does something like this even sell these days?

593
00:36:53,750 --> 00:36:55,280
- Ma'am. - Yes?

594
00:36:57,420 --> 00:36:58,490
The car is waiting.

595
00:37:00,490 --> 00:37:01,660
How do I look today, Director Kang?

596
00:37:02,960 --> 00:37:05,460
- Did you just yawn? - Please.

597
00:37:08,160 --> 00:37:09,200
Look again, carefully.

598
00:37:11,000 --> 00:37:13,200
- Forget it. The contract. - You're... Yes, ma'am.

599
00:37:14,800 --> 00:37:17,309
I feel fluttered because...

600
00:37:17,310 --> 00:37:18,310
it's been a while since I had to go out and hustle.

601
00:37:19,740 --> 00:37:20,740
- Let's move out. - Yes, ma'am.

602
00:37:21,310 --> 00:37:23,510
(Top Line Entertainment)

603
00:37:30,420 --> 00:37:32,020
- Let's go. - Yes, ma'am.

604
00:37:45,470 --> 00:37:47,470
I think she's gone now.

605
00:37:49,070 --> 00:37:50,140
Okay.

606
00:38:22,470 --> 00:38:23,970
(Oh Ha Na)

607
00:38:34,150 --> 00:38:36,150
(Exclusive Artist Contract)

608
00:38:52,470 --> 00:38:55,440
(Gyeongseong Love Song)

609
00:38:56,070 --> 00:38:57,610
Gyeongseong Love Song?

610
00:39:14,890 --> 00:39:16,859
Wolhwajeong, where only a sliver of moonlight...

611
00:39:16,860 --> 00:39:18,060
has settled.

612
00:39:19,260 --> 00:39:22,030
In the middle of the darkness stands Nan Yeong.

613
00:39:32,410 --> 00:39:33,410
Nan Yeong.

614
00:39:34,410 --> 00:39:36,050
After catching her breath,

615
00:39:36,110 --> 00:39:38,680
she sets down the heavy bag she's holding...

616
00:39:39,350 --> 00:39:40,680
and takes something out.

617
00:39:42,590 --> 00:39:45,620
In her trembling hands, she's holding dynamite.

618
00:39:49,190 --> 00:39:50,630
She already made up her mind.

619
00:39:52,230 --> 00:39:54,299
The moment she ignites this fuse...

620
00:39:54,300 --> 00:39:56,069
(It will be aired on Friday, 10pm.)

621
00:39:56,070 --> 00:39:57,630
will start everything.

622
00:40:01,470 --> 00:40:03,870
Nan Yeong hides explosives all around Wolhwajeong,

623
00:40:05,010 --> 00:40:06,640
then stands, gripping the fuse tightly.

624
00:40:08,310 --> 00:40:11,650
Beneath the wall, Nan Yeong's face, illuminated by the flame of a match,

625
00:40:11,810 --> 00:40:13,250
flickers with a red glow.

626
00:40:19,420 --> 00:40:22,660
Tonight, Nan Yeong will explode Wolhwajeong.

627
00:40:24,830 --> 00:40:27,960
I finally understand. The high walls of Wolhwajeong...

628
00:40:28,030 --> 00:40:29,970
weren't a fence meant to protect me.

629
00:40:30,700 --> 00:40:32,430
They were the bars of a cage that imprisoned me.

630
00:40:33,740 --> 00:40:36,370
Now, I will smash it all with my own hands.

631
00:40:54,160 --> 00:40:55,160
Let's go, Chae Yeon.

632
00:41:01,700 --> 00:41:03,830
I found it. The way out.

633
00:41:08,240 --> 00:41:09,340
Take your time.

634
00:41:11,840 --> 00:41:13,540
Oh, it's fine.

635
00:41:14,780 --> 00:41:15,810
I'm okay.

636
00:41:19,010 --> 00:41:20,020
So,

637
00:41:21,820 --> 00:41:22,890
have you made a decision?

638
00:41:24,690 --> 00:41:25,990
I'm a little impatient.

639
00:41:27,890 --> 00:41:28,890
Ma'am,

640
00:41:29,560 --> 00:41:31,160
I want to be successful.

641
00:41:33,930 --> 00:41:34,960
Within a month...

642
00:41:37,070 --> 00:41:38,230
Is that possible?

643
00:41:41,440 --> 00:41:42,840
I told you I'm impatient.

644
00:41:47,180 --> 00:41:49,910
(Exclusive Artist Contract)

645
00:42:03,460 --> 00:42:04,790
How are you feeling today?

646
00:42:07,030 --> 00:42:10,230
I can't tell if this is real or if I'm dreaming.

647
00:42:12,100 --> 00:42:13,100
But...

648
00:42:13,970 --> 00:42:15,200
it's our first get-together,

649
00:42:15,470 --> 00:42:17,170
but I guess our boss decided not to show up.

650
00:42:17,340 --> 00:42:20,310
- He's filming a dating show today. - A dating show?

651
00:42:20,410 --> 00:42:21,510
A dating show.

652
00:42:24,210 --> 00:42:25,920
Seriously, what is he doing?

653
00:42:26,650 --> 00:42:27,650
Well, whatever.

654
00:42:27,720 --> 00:42:29,520
As long as I have the corporate card.

655
00:42:29,990 --> 00:42:32,190
But he said you'd be paying for it.

656
00:42:33,060 --> 00:42:35,890
- Me? - He said to keep the receipt.

657
00:42:36,730 --> 00:42:39,060
Is he trying to make me go broke?

658
00:42:41,600 --> 00:42:43,000
Oh, Director Joo.

659
00:42:45,170 --> 00:42:46,799
- Hello. - Hello.

660
00:42:46,800 --> 00:42:49,100
- Hello. - Hello.

661
00:42:49,170 --> 00:42:50,270
Hello.

662
00:42:51,970 --> 00:42:53,010
Let's drink.

663
00:42:53,310 --> 00:42:55,280
- Cheers. - Cheers.

664
00:42:56,110 --> 00:42:57,710
- Cheers. - Cheers.

665
00:43:04,990 --> 00:43:07,760
- Cheers. - Cheers.

666
00:43:14,560 --> 00:43:16,299
Hey, Gwang Il. I heard Director Seo is filming...

667
00:43:16,300 --> 00:43:18,800
on Yulgokdo Island right now. Isn't that place close to here?

668
00:43:19,340 --> 00:43:21,640
You're thinking of going? Gosh, don't even think about it.

669
00:43:21,670 --> 00:43:23,110
I heard it's total chaos over there.

670
00:43:23,340 --> 00:43:24,809
One wrong move and your name will end up...

671
00:43:24,810 --> 00:43:26,080
in the credits for that film, DP.

672
00:43:26,140 --> 00:43:27,609
Yes, I heard it's a total boot camp over there.

673
00:43:27,610 --> 00:43:29,109
The crew is ready to build a raft...

674
00:43:29,110 --> 00:43:30,810
to get out of there. It's absolute chaos.

675
00:43:31,350 --> 00:43:34,480
You're talking about Director Seo Dong Yoon, right?

676
00:43:34,550 --> 00:43:36,920
He's famous for being incredibly demanding, isn't he?

677
00:43:36,990 --> 00:43:38,620
I hear it's one of the toughest sets to be on.

678
00:43:38,690 --> 00:43:40,290
That's the rumour going around.

679
00:43:44,590 --> 00:43:45,590
Director Joo.

680
00:43:46,230 --> 00:43:47,730
Are you a bit soft, Director Joo?

681
00:43:48,930 --> 00:43:51,900
A director is supposed to be demanding.

682
00:43:52,100 --> 00:43:54,540
That's why Director Seo is where he is today.

683
00:43:54,740 --> 00:43:56,439
That's why the crew members who survive his sets...

684
00:43:56,440 --> 00:43:58,540
wear it like a badge of honour.

685
00:43:59,170 --> 00:44:01,110
Exactly. It's a point of pride for them.

686
00:44:02,680 --> 00:44:05,350
Oh, there you are, Art Director.

687
00:44:06,250 --> 00:44:08,480
Why are you sitting all the way over here in the corner?

688
00:44:09,490 --> 00:44:11,850
Art Director, you went to Seonghwa University, right?

689
00:44:12,350 --> 00:44:14,590
So you're my senior from school. Should I call you Namgung?

690
00:44:14,720 --> 00:44:17,060
Just call me Se Ra.

691
00:44:17,130 --> 00:44:18,260
Yes, Se Ra.

692
00:44:18,690 --> 00:44:19,899
I'm Ryu Sang Mok.

693
00:44:19,900 --> 00:44:21,900
Theater and Film major, class of 2006, Seonghwa University.

694
00:44:22,400 --> 00:44:24,130
I don't have much school spirit.

695
00:44:24,400 --> 00:44:26,570
Then maybe you'll take a liking to me?

696
00:44:27,370 --> 00:44:30,910
- Hey there. - Wait, who are you talking to?

697
00:44:34,580 --> 00:44:35,940
Drink up, drink up.

698
00:44:36,710 --> 00:44:37,710
Drink up.

699
00:44:39,280 --> 00:44:40,280
Cheers.

700
00:44:41,080 --> 00:44:42,220
And what about Director Joo?

701
00:44:42,750 --> 00:44:44,049
- Yes? - Which university...

702
00:44:44,050 --> 00:44:45,050
did you graduate from?

703
00:44:47,020 --> 00:44:50,590
I mean, why'd you become a reporter instead of using your major?

704
00:44:51,890 --> 00:44:54,029
I was...

705
00:44:54,030 --> 00:44:55,100
Hey, cheers, everyone.

706
00:44:57,200 --> 00:44:58,570
- Drink up. - Beer, beer, beer.

707
00:44:58,730 --> 00:45:00,600
- Here you go. - Cheers.

708
00:45:03,170 --> 00:45:05,110
Please give me one more...

709
00:45:11,150 --> 00:45:13,980
Life's so unfair, isn't it?

710
00:45:14,450 --> 00:45:15,850
Tell me about it.

711
00:45:16,220 --> 00:45:18,889
Someone works himself to the bone in this industry for 13 years.

712
00:45:18,890 --> 00:45:20,020
Yet, he doesn't have his own work.

713
00:45:20,420 --> 00:45:22,120
Hey, Five-Year.

714
00:45:23,260 --> 00:45:25,130
That's a very specific number.

715
00:45:25,990 --> 00:45:27,130
Are you talking about me?

716
00:45:27,500 --> 00:45:28,660
I'm just saying...

717
00:45:29,130 --> 00:45:32,300
With all these legendary veterans still in the game,

718
00:45:32,370 --> 00:45:33,840
some nobody...

719
00:45:34,000 --> 00:45:35,400
- Right? - True.

720
00:45:35,570 --> 00:45:37,140
That's what I'm saying.

721
00:45:37,710 --> 00:45:39,440
What a life.

722
00:45:41,080 --> 00:45:42,180
I have to pee.

723
00:45:44,810 --> 00:45:47,379
- This can't be right, can it? - You're right.

724
00:45:47,380 --> 00:45:49,720
Okay, she's a former reporter.

725
00:45:50,320 --> 00:45:52,790
Fine, I'll give her that.

726
00:45:53,320 --> 00:45:56,190
But she's never even studied film.

727
00:45:56,460 --> 00:46:00,100
But there are plenty of directors who didn't major in film, you know?

728
00:46:00,430 --> 00:46:01,900
Hey.

729
00:46:02,460 --> 00:46:05,030
There's a big difference between them and her.

730
00:46:05,570 --> 00:46:07,700
It's not like she went to some top-tier schools.

731
00:46:07,770 --> 00:46:09,470
Just some grad from a no-name university...

732
00:46:10,340 --> 00:46:13,540
waltzes in here, not knowing her place.

733
00:46:13,940 --> 00:46:16,410
Hey, what the heck? Why isn't anyone coming out?

734
00:46:16,480 --> 00:46:19,620
- You'll be in there all day? - No, no, stop.

735
00:46:19,680 --> 00:46:22,020
- Should I just kick it down? - You shouldn't do that.

736
00:46:22,820 --> 00:46:24,550
Hey, no, don't.

737
00:46:24,920 --> 00:46:26,820
Hey, come on. You're too drunk.

738
00:46:26,860 --> 00:46:27,860
Why are you crying?

739
00:46:27,920 --> 00:46:29,460
- What's wrong with you? - I'm not crying.

740
00:46:29,790 --> 00:46:31,390
Do you own the toilet? Get out now.

741
00:46:31,460 --> 00:46:33,130
- Just a minute. - Hey. Get out.

742
00:46:33,200 --> 00:46:34,660
- No. - Hey.

743
00:46:34,730 --> 00:46:36,370
- Hey, hey, hey. - Do you even know who I am?

744
00:46:36,430 --> 00:46:38,870
- Hey. You really have to pee. - You little punk.

745
00:46:38,930 --> 00:46:40,670
- I'm sorry. I'm sorry. - What...

746
00:46:41,170 --> 00:46:42,270
Director.

747
00:46:43,470 --> 00:46:44,470
What the...

748
00:46:47,410 --> 00:46:51,050
(Restroom)

749
00:46:51,180 --> 00:46:52,180
Hey.

750
00:46:53,020 --> 00:46:55,620
Seriously, what are we going to do? Gosh.

751
00:46:55,680 --> 00:46:57,649
I just said the truth...

752
00:46:57,650 --> 00:46:58,719
- about her educational background. - Yi Jae.

753
00:46:58,720 --> 00:47:01,260
- Hey, man. Hey. - Restroom? Someone was in there.

754
00:47:01,320 --> 00:47:02,990
Please keep it down.

755
00:47:03,060 --> 00:47:04,960
I'm talking loudly so she can hear me, right?

756
00:47:05,030 --> 00:47:08,660
How is it possible? I'm the one who majored in it, and she's not.

757
00:47:08,730 --> 00:47:11,400
- Please, man, please. - I want to be a director.

758
00:47:11,470 --> 00:47:13,000
What's wrong with you?

759
00:47:13,300 --> 00:47:14,900
This is my first time, so...

760
00:47:15,470 --> 00:47:18,070
Honestly, it's true. I'll need a lot of your help.

761
00:47:18,340 --> 00:47:19,810
- Of course. - I'm counting on you all.

762
00:47:19,880 --> 00:47:21,680
We look forward to working with you.

763
00:47:24,550 --> 00:47:25,710
I think I'm drunk...

764
00:47:27,020 --> 00:47:28,450
Have you tried this? It's really delicious.

765
00:47:28,520 --> 00:47:30,950
- Director Woo. Come have a drink. - Let's drink together.

766
00:47:31,020 --> 00:47:32,790
- Have a drink. - Come over here.

767
00:47:32,850 --> 00:47:33,890
Great, great.

768
00:47:34,490 --> 00:47:37,660
- Now that our director's here. - Cheers.

769
00:47:38,590 --> 00:47:40,360
- This too. - It's delicious?

770
00:47:40,430 --> 00:47:41,430
It's really good.

771
00:47:44,030 --> 00:47:45,270
You should've called me.

772
00:47:45,330 --> 00:47:46,340
I should've at least called...

773
00:47:49,970 --> 00:47:51,640
Producer, I'm going to head out now.

774
00:47:51,710 --> 00:47:54,010
Are you heading home? Do you need a ride?

775
00:47:54,080 --> 00:47:57,110
- No, I already called a cab. - Okay, get home safe.

776
00:47:57,180 --> 00:47:59,480
- Thank you. - Get home safe.

777
00:48:00,480 --> 00:48:02,050
- Well then... - Where are you going?

778
00:48:02,120 --> 00:48:04,920
- Hey, man. Hey. - Let's go for a second round.

779
00:48:05,390 --> 00:48:06,560
- Hey. - Let's go for a second round.

780
00:48:06,620 --> 00:48:08,890
- No, no. - Let's go for a second round.

781
00:48:08,960 --> 00:48:10,430
- No. - Let's go for a second round.

782
00:48:13,830 --> 00:48:16,100
(A Lavish Feast)

783
00:48:28,840 --> 00:48:29,910
Hello, Director.

784
00:48:30,680 --> 00:48:32,409
- When did you get here? - Assistant Director.

785
00:48:32,410 --> 00:48:33,749
Yes.

786
00:48:33,750 --> 00:48:37,720
This will be the first and last time that I explain my decisions.

787
00:48:38,150 --> 00:48:39,150
Pardon?

788
00:48:39,720 --> 00:48:41,120
What are you... What are you trying to say...

789
00:48:41,890 --> 00:48:43,090
Yi Jae wrote "Gyeongseong Love Song..."

790
00:48:43,160 --> 00:48:44,260
when she was a senior in high school.

791
00:48:45,330 --> 00:48:47,930
That's why I'm letting Yi Jae handle all the script meetings.

792
00:48:49,130 --> 00:48:50,969
I decided it would be more efficient for me...

793
00:48:50,970 --> 00:48:52,300
to handle the location hunting in the meantime.

794
00:48:53,840 --> 00:48:55,170
- Oh, right. - Assistant Director.

795
00:48:56,200 --> 00:48:59,270
Director Joo Yi Jae is doing her job perfectly.

796
00:49:02,710 --> 00:49:05,380
- Yes, she is. - Does this make you uncomfortable?

797
00:49:06,210 --> 00:49:07,420
No, Director.

798
00:49:08,750 --> 00:49:09,890
Oh, no. That's not it at all.

799
00:49:11,650 --> 00:49:12,650
I'm sorry.

800
00:49:13,890 --> 00:49:15,260
You don't owe me an apology.

801
00:49:16,930 --> 00:49:18,530
From now on, let's all...

802
00:49:19,590 --> 00:49:20,830
just do our own part...

803
00:49:22,000 --> 00:49:23,070
while respecting one another.

804
00:49:23,330 --> 00:49:25,030
- Yes. - Enjoy your meal.

805
00:49:26,500 --> 00:49:29,470
(A Lavish Feast)

806
00:49:29,870 --> 00:49:30,870
You're back?

807
00:49:32,210 --> 00:49:33,210
- Ma'am. - Yes?

808
00:49:33,211 --> 00:49:34,910
Please put the staff's meal on my tab.

809
00:49:35,540 --> 00:49:36,750
You're paying for everyone?

810
00:49:37,650 --> 00:49:38,750
My goodness.

811
00:50:05,610 --> 00:50:08,410
No, no one has said anything.

812
00:50:08,910 --> 00:50:10,180
Don't you find that strange?

813
00:50:11,180 --> 00:50:12,380
No one asks who I am,

814
00:50:12,510 --> 00:50:15,220
and how or why I'm here as a director.

815
00:50:15,280 --> 00:50:18,020
I just said the truth about her educational background.

816
00:50:18,090 --> 00:50:20,759
- Hey, man. Hey. - It's...

817
00:50:20,760 --> 00:50:22,590
Please keep it down.

818
00:50:22,660 --> 00:50:24,589
I'm talking loudly so she can hear me, right?

819
00:50:24,590 --> 00:50:26,500
I'm the one who majored in it...

820
00:50:35,240 --> 00:50:37,970
- Hello? - Where are you? We need to talk.

821
00:50:38,970 --> 00:50:40,180
I'm right in front of your place.

822
00:50:40,840 --> 00:50:43,350
(Jaejae Noodles)

823
00:50:54,390 --> 00:50:55,390
What are you doing?

824
00:50:56,660 --> 00:50:57,660
Just watch.

825
00:50:59,060 --> 00:51:00,600
- Why are you running? - Just stay there and watch.

826
00:51:06,070 --> 00:51:08,640
See? I can run like this, and I'm perfectly fine.

827
00:51:08,870 --> 00:51:10,010
It doesn't hurt at all.

828
00:52:32,150 --> 00:52:33,190
You know...

829
00:52:33,920 --> 00:52:36,120
You know what my life has been like.

830
00:52:38,960 --> 00:52:42,300
I've spent entire days stuck in mudflats,

831
00:52:44,300 --> 00:52:46,370
and climbed countless mountains.

832
00:53:04,150 --> 00:53:05,350
So please, stop it.

833
00:53:07,620 --> 00:53:09,190
Because of you, I feel my scars...

834
00:53:10,930 --> 00:53:12,460
are becoming obvious.

835
00:53:18,400 --> 00:53:20,400
If you really feel sorry for me,

836
00:53:21,900 --> 00:53:23,540
if you pity me so much,

837
00:53:26,340 --> 00:53:28,310
then please recognise that I'm here now...

838
00:53:30,010 --> 00:53:31,710
despite everything that happened.

839
00:53:35,150 --> 00:53:36,590
And please understand what I was feeling...

840
00:53:38,850 --> 00:53:42,120
when I finally made it here.

841
00:53:45,130 --> 00:53:46,600
I really want to do a good job.

842
00:53:47,560 --> 00:53:48,700
I don't want to have any more regrets.

843
00:53:55,440 --> 00:53:56,540
So help me, Woo Su Bin.

844
00:53:58,610 --> 00:54:00,010
So I can start running again.

845
00:54:04,180 --> 00:54:05,250
What's your dream?

846
00:54:05,580 --> 00:54:07,649
To be a film director.

847
00:54:07,650 --> 00:54:09,050
Hurry up, come on.

848
00:54:10,250 --> 00:54:11,790
So? Pretty cool, right?

849
00:54:17,760 --> 00:54:21,130
I, Joo Yi Jae, will become a humane film director.

850
00:54:22,200 --> 00:54:23,630
Go, Joo Yi Jae.

851
00:54:26,970 --> 00:54:29,240
Let's make movies together.

852
00:54:30,240 --> 00:54:32,470
Let's do something great together.

853
00:54:35,880 --> 00:54:36,880
A romance.

854
00:54:37,380 --> 00:54:41,520
Let's write a romance together. We'll write an amazing romance plot.

855
00:55:03,770 --> 00:55:05,540
I admired you so much.

856
00:55:07,610 --> 00:55:09,040
This bright, shining face of yours.

857
00:55:21,260 --> 00:55:22,360
That's why I like you.

858
00:55:23,120 --> 00:55:24,130
Yi Jae.

859
00:55:46,480 --> 00:55:47,480
This is something I should have done...

860
00:55:49,050 --> 00:55:50,250
when we were 19.

861
00:56:09,670 --> 00:56:10,710
I'll stop...

862
00:56:11,840 --> 00:56:12,840
here.

863
00:56:16,040 --> 00:56:17,380
So you can shine brighter.

864
00:56:19,280 --> 00:56:20,820
I never thought that my feelings for you...

865
00:56:21,620 --> 00:56:23,990
would become a burden to you.

866
00:56:25,250 --> 00:56:26,250
I'm sorry.

867
00:56:27,660 --> 00:56:28,660
No.

868
00:56:31,190 --> 00:56:34,330
No, I wasn't asking for an apology.

869
00:56:35,030 --> 00:56:36,500
I was just asking you to help me.

870
00:56:38,500 --> 00:56:39,500
I'm sorry...

871
00:56:40,970 --> 00:56:42,240
that this is the best I can do.

872
00:56:44,910 --> 00:56:45,970
Anyway...

873
00:56:46,940 --> 00:56:50,250
What's important is that we finish the movie together.

874
00:56:52,050 --> 00:56:53,050
Still...

875
00:56:53,620 --> 00:56:55,220
Give me some time to sort out my feelings.

876
00:56:59,750 --> 00:57:02,020
Then until the revised script is ready,

877
00:57:02,620 --> 00:57:04,230
I'll work from home.

878
00:57:05,790 --> 00:57:06,800
Take care.

879
00:57:10,600 --> 00:57:11,600
What?

880
00:57:12,230 --> 00:57:13,370
Why does that sound like a final goodbye?

881
00:57:13,800 --> 00:57:15,140
It is a final goodbye.

882
00:57:16,340 --> 00:57:17,340
To my first love.

883
00:57:19,070 --> 00:57:22,610
When the revised script is ready, let's meet as colleagues.

884
00:57:25,610 --> 00:57:28,020
Oh, so that's how it is?

885
00:57:28,380 --> 00:57:29,380
Yes.

886
00:57:31,620 --> 00:57:32,620
Well then...

887
00:57:33,620 --> 00:57:35,590
Goodbye, Yi Jae.

888
00:57:36,520 --> 00:57:37,530
Yes.

889
00:57:38,260 --> 00:57:39,260
See you soon,

890
00:57:39,790 --> 00:57:40,800
Director Joo.

891
00:57:41,960 --> 00:57:42,960
I'm going.

892
00:58:48,130 --> 00:58:50,060
(Dream To You)

893
00:58:50,830 --> 00:58:51,900
Director Joo Yi Jae.

894
00:58:52,900 --> 00:58:55,600
I really want to be in that movie.

895
00:58:55,670 --> 00:58:57,770
- Is someone else coming? - Sim Yu Geon.

896
00:58:57,940 --> 00:58:59,470
- Su Bin. - What do you think you're doing?

897
00:58:59,540 --> 00:59:02,380
Are you casting Sim Yu Geon or dropping Joo Yi Jae?

898
00:59:02,540 --> 00:59:05,280
It's uncomfortable and unpleasant when you show up unannounced.

899
00:59:05,480 --> 00:59:07,650
It's creating so much buzz. The moment the Catfish entered,

900
00:59:07,720 --> 00:59:09,020
the entire vibe changed.

901
00:59:09,250 --> 00:59:10,550
Why does it feel like it went by in a flash?

902
00:59:10,620 --> 00:59:11,650
The time I waited for you was longer...

903
00:59:11,720 --> 00:59:13,050
Well, I'll be on my way.

904
00:59:13,120 --> 00:59:15,320
Then what were we? What were we back then?

905
00:59:16,060 --> 00:59:17,260
I think it was love.